---
import '../styles/landing.css';
import Feature from '../components/Feature.astro';
import logo from '../assets/logo.png';
import mark from '../assets/logo-mark.png';

const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/?$/, '/');
const shot = (name: string) => `${base}shots/${name}.webp`;
const thumb = (name: string) => `${base}shots/${name}-thumb.webp`;
---

<html lang="en">
	<head>
		<meta charset="utf-8" />
		<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
		<title>Screensemble — Signage That Takes the Stage.</title>
		<meta
			name="description"
			content="Screensemble is a self-hosted, offline-first digital signage system. Every display always shows an intentional state — no blanks, no launchers, no waiting. Runs on Kodi, managed from one dashboard."
		/>
		<link rel="icon" type="image/png" href={`${base}favicon.png`} />
	</head>
	<body>
		<nav class="top-nav">
			<a href={`${base}docs/`}>Docs</a>
		</nav>
		<header class="hero">
			<img class="hero-icon" src={logo.src} alt="Screensemble logo — a conductor leading a fan of screens" width="148" height="148" />
			<h1>Screensemble</h1>
			<p class="hero-eyebrow">Digital signage system</p>
			<p class="tagline">Signage That Takes the Stage.</p>
			<p class="sub">
				An ensemble of screens — self-hosted, offline-first displays that
				always show an intentional state. No blank walls, no launchers, no
				waiting screens. Runs on Kodi, conducted from one dashboard.
			</p>
			<div class="hero-actions">
				<a class="btn btn-primary" href={`${base}docs/getting-started/`}>Get started</a>
				<a class="btn btn-ghost" href="https://github.com/Screensemble">
					<svg width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 16 16" fill="currentColor" aria-hidden="true">
						<path d="M8 0C3.58 0 0 3.58 0 8c0 3.54 2.29 6.53 5.47 7.59.4.07.55-.17.55-.38 0-.19-.01-.82-.01-1.49-2.01.37-2.53-.49-2.69-.94-.09-.23-.48-.94-.82-1.13-.28-.15-.68-.52-.01-.53.63-.01 1.08.58 1.23.82.72 1.21 1.87.87 2.33.66.07-.52.28-.87.51-1.07-1.78-.2-3.64-.89-3.64-3.95 0-.87.31-1.59.82-2.15-.08-.2-.36-1.02.08-2.12 0 0 .67-.21 2.2.82.64-.18 1.32-.27 2-.27s1.36.09 2 .27c1.53-1.04 2.2-.82 2.2-.82.44 1.1.16 1.92.08 2.12.51.56.82 1.27.82 2.15 0 3.07-1.87 3.75-3.65 3.95.29.25.54.73.54 1.48 0 1.07-.01 1.93-.01 2.2 0 .21.15.46.55.38A8.01 8.01 0 0 0 16 8c0-4.42-3.58-8-8-8Z" />
					</svg>
					GitHub
				</a>
			</div>
			<svg class="scroll-cue" width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true">
				<path d="m6 9 6 6 6-6" />
			</svg>
		</header>

		<main class="features">
			<Feature
				kicker="Always intentional"
				title="Never a blank, never a launcher"
				shot={shot('standby')}
				alt="A display in Screensemble's branded standby state"
			>
				The moment playback ends, most signage shows you its seams — a media
				player home screen, an Android launcher, a black wall. Screensemble
				shows none of it. Every display always presents a deliberate state:
				your content, or a branded standby.
				<ul slot="points">
					<li>A resident idle window sits beneath playback — the OS and player UI never surface</li>
					<li>The next image is preloaded during video — zero black on every transition</li>
					<li>Standby keeps a dim mark on screen while a playlist is empty</li>
				</ul>
			</Feature>

			<Feature
				kicker="One playlist"
				title="Images, videos and streams — in order"
				flip
				shot={shot('promo1')}
				alt="A display showing a Screensemble playlist slide"
			>
				One sequence that treats every media type the same. Images hold for
				their own durations, videos play end-to-end, live streams sit
				alongside both. Set order, timing, shuffle and schedules — then walk
				away.
				<ul slot="points">
					<li>Per-item durations, dates, weekdays and time windows</li>
					<li>Back-to-back videos chain inside the player — the seam is invisible</li>
					<li>Updates land at the natural end of the current piece, never mid-play</li>
				</ul>
			</Feature>

			<Feature
				kicker="One dashboard"
				title="Every screen in the fleet"
				shot={undefined}
				alt="Screensemble fleet dashboard"
			>
				Pair each display once and it registers itself with a hardware-anchored
				identity — reinstalls and wipes rebind to the same screen instead of
				minting duplicates. Watch status, push content, manage each device
				from the server.
				<ul slot="points">
					<li>Per-device pairing tokens — a spoofed ID can't hijack a display</li>
					<li>Health, now-playing and link state, live over a persistent connection</li>
					<li>A full per-display admin panel mirrors the on-device UI</li>
				</ul>
				<div slot="mock" class="mock-fleet">
					<div class="mock-fleet-head">
						<img src={mark.src} alt="" />
						Screensemble — displays
					</div>
					<div class="mock-row"><span class="mock-dot on"></span>Gallery North<em>Playing · promo2.png</em></div>
					<div class="mock-row"><span class="mock-dot on"></span>Gallery South<em>Playing · intro.mp4</em></div>
					<div class="mock-row"><span class="mock-dot on"></span>Lobby Wall<em>Standby</em></div>
					<div class="mock-row"><span class="mock-dot off"></span>Studio Annex<em>Last seen 2h ago</em></div>
				</div>
			</Feature>

			<Feature
				kicker="Shared content"
				title="A library every display draws from"
				flip
				alt="Screensemble media library"
			>
				The server keeps every file you've pushed, so content is never trapped
				on one screen. Build named playlists out of library items, assign them
				to displays, and sync — missing files push down, extras can be pruned,
				order applies everywhere.
				<ul slot="points">
					<li>Upload once, reuse across any display</li>
					<li>Exact-match sync makes every assigned screen identical</li>
					<li>SHA-256 verified transfers — corrupt files never go live</li>
				</ul>
				<div slot="mock" class="mock-library">
					<div class="mock-fleet-head">
						<img src={mark.src} alt="" />
						Library — Gallery Loop
					</div>
					<div class="mock-grid">
						<div class="mock-tile sync"><img src={thumb('promo1')} alt="" /><span>promo1.png</span></div>
						<div class="mock-tile sync"><img src={thumb('promo2')} alt="" /><span>promo2.png</span></div>
						<div class="mock-tile sync"><img src={thumb('promo3')} alt="" /><span>promo3.png</span></div>
						<div class="mock-tile"><img src={thumb('standby')} alt="" /><span>intro.mp4</span></div>
						<div class="mock-tile"><img src={thumb('promo1')} alt="" /><span>gallery.mp4</span></div>
						<div class="mock-tile"><img src={thumb('promo2')} alt="" /><span>tour.mp4</span></div>
					</div>
				</div>
			</Feature>

			<Feature
				kicker="Offline-proof"
				title="The show goes on without the network"
				shot={shot('promo2')}
				alt="A display continuing to play cached content offline"
			>
				Every display caches what it needs locally and keeps playing through
				server restarts, dead links and dead routers. Content changes queue
				in the background and land at the next natural boundary — a video's
				end, an image's timer.
				<ul slot="points">
					<li>Local mode runs a full playlist with zero server at all</li>
					<li>Cache cap with least-recently-used eviction — no manual cleanup</li>
					<li>A stall watchdog skips frozen video instead of staring at it</li>
				</ul>
			</Feature>
		</main>

		<section class="wrapup reveal">
			<p>An ensemble of screens, playing in concert.</p>
			<h2 class="wrapup-title">Ready to raise the curtain?</h2>
			<div class="hero-actions">
				<a class="btn btn-primary" href={`${base}docs/getting-started/`}>Get started</a>
				<a class="btn btn-ghost" href={`${base}docs/`}>Documentation</a>
			</div>
		</section>

		<footer class="site-footer">
			<p>
				<strong>Screensemble</strong> — <em>An ensemble of screens.</em><br />
				Free, open-source, self-hosted software. Your content stays on your
				own hardware.
			</p>
			<p>
				<a href={`${base}docs/getting-started/`}>Get Started</a>
				&nbsp;·&nbsp;
				<a href="https://github.com/Screensemble/Screensemble-Server">Server</a>
				&nbsp;·&nbsp;
				<a href="https://github.com/Screensemble/Screensemble-Addon">Kodi Player</a>
				&nbsp;·&nbsp;
				<a href={`${base}docs/`}>Documentation</a>
			</p>
		</footer>

		<script is:inline>
			document.documentElement.classList.add('js');
			const io = 'IntersectionObserver' in window
				? new IntersectionObserver(
						(entries) => {
							for (const e of entries) {
								if (e.isIntersecting) {
									e.target.classList.add('visible');
									io.unobserve(e.target);
								}
							}
						},
						{ threshold: 0.2, rootMargin: '0px 0px -8% 0px' }
					)
				: null;
			document
				.querySelectorAll('.reveal')
				.forEach((el) => (io ? io.observe(el) : el.classList.add('visible')));
		</script>
	</body>
</html>
